    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"1. Geographic assignment\"\nsubtitle: \"Using the assignR package to estimate geographic origin\"\ndescription: \"Using the assignR package to estimate geographic origin\"\ndate-modified: last-modified\n---\n\n::: {.callout-note appearance=\"simple\" icon=\"false\"}\n## In this section\n\n-   **You'll learn:** the key idea or skill\n-   **You'll need:** packages or data from earlier sections\n-   **Time:** about 30 minutes\n:::\n\n## Overview\n\nA short introduction to the topic: why it matters and what we're going to do.\n\n## Setting up\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(tidyverse)\nlibrary(assignR)\nlibrary(raster)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Unknown origin data\n\nExplain the idea in a sentence or two, then show the code.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmtcars |>\n  group_by(cyl) |>\n  summarise(mean_mpg = mean(mpg))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<div data-pagedtable=\"false\">\n  <script data-pagedtable-source type=\"application/json\">\n{\"columns\":[{\"label\":[\"cyl\"],\"name\":[1],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"mean_mpg\"],\"name\":[2],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]}],\"data\":[{\"1\":\"4\",\"2\":\"26.66364\"},{\"1\":\"6\",\"2\":\"19.74286\"},{\"1\":\"8\",\"2\":\"15.10000\"}],\"options\":{\"columns\":{\"min\":{},\"max\":[10]},\"rows\":{\"min\":[10],\"max\":[10]},\"pages\":{}}}\n  </script>\n</div>\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: callout-tip\n## Tip\n\nA helpful shortcut or good-practice note.\n:::\n\n### A sub-step\n\nUse `###` headings for smaller steps. They appear nested in the table of contents.\n\n## Strontium isoscape\n\nTabsets are handy for showing alternatives side by side:\n\n::: panel-tabset\n## tidyverse\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmtcars |> filter(mpg > 25)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<div data-pagedtable=\"false\">\n  <script data-pagedtable-source type=\"application/json\">\n{\"columns\":[{\"label\":[\"\"],\"name\":[\"_